Falsifies `paging::sv39::verification::no_encoded_leaf_is_both_writable_and_executable`.

The defect: `Sv39::attrs` sets `X` on a writable page as well, on the reasoning that the U bit
already decides which privilege may execute it. U does not make the page non-executable, it only
picks who executes it, and a leaf with W and X both set is exactly the page W^X refuses.

Expected to fail: `assert!(leaf & (1 << 2) == 0 || leaf & (1 << 3) == 0)`, the harness's only
assertion, on `Flags::kernel_data()` and `Flags::user_data()`.

